[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0f408c7cc77c9614016a35ad7c4944819094e6eacca8551395","text":"Implemented the schematic-only tscircuit project in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx).\n\nWhat’s included:\n- USB-C PD input modeled around `STUSB4500`\n- Negotiated VBUS power path with fuse, TVS, and load switch\n- `LM3409HV` constant-current buck LED driver\n- Analog-filtered dimming path plus high-frequency `PWM_DIM` enable for video-safe dimming\n- MCU control, frame sync input, SWD header, NTC thermal foldback, and LED ring connector\n- `routingDisabled` set on the board\n- No tscircuit registry component imports\n\nVerification:\n- `npm run typecheck` passes\n- `tsci check schematic-placement` passes cleanly\n- `tsci build` writes `dist/index/circuit.json` and exits `0`, but reports schematic-test warnings around connector edge orientation, missing `pinAttributes`, and approximate JLC supplier-footprint mismatches.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: `schDisplayValue` is used in the installed example but rejected by current TypeScript types for most components.\n- Wasted most time: resolving contradictory schematic checker guidance for the built-in USB-C `standard=\"usb_c\"` symbol; shrinking fixed pin padding but caused inner-label collisions.\n- Helpful docs/tooling changes: clearer docs for valid footprint strings, connector pin labels, and which props are supported per component type.\n- Specific friction: JLC supplier part numbers often produced footprint mismatch or fetch warnings even for schematic-only work, and `tsci build` prints “completed with errors” while still exiting successfully.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019ee1a7-4e6e-7ec0-82f5-d72d46730548","turnId":"019ee1a7-4ea4-72d3-b2a6-b7ae51e3a599","completedAtMs":1781902722437}}
